WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:19.728
This lesson follows the teaching themes of school 1B: foundations, communication, partnership, cultural humility and trauma-informed practice. Our scenarios and reflection exercises are original preparations for those skills, not reproductions of the school competency checks or their answers.
本课依学校1B教学主题展开：基础概念、沟通、伙伴关系、文化谦逊及创伤知情实践。情景与反思练习是为这些技能编写的原创准备，不是复制学校能力考核或其答案。

00:00:19.728 --> 00:00:31.344
The central question is not whether the clinician intended respect. It is whether the patient experienced dignity, choice, understanding and safety while receiving needed care.
核心问题不是医护人员是否“本意尊重”，而是患者在获得所需照护时，是否实际感受到尊严、选择、理解与安全。

00:00:31.344 --> 00:00:42.456
Cultural humility is an ongoing practice of self-reflection, listening and learning. It is not a badge a clinician earns or a claim to understand another person completely.
文化谦逊是持续的自我反思、倾听与学习，不是医护人员获得的徽章，也不代表自己完全理解他人。

00:00:42.456 --> 00:00:56.928
Cultural safety focuses on the person receiving care and on power. Equity asks what unequal barriers need to change. Anti-racism requires action when racism is interpersonal or built into a process.
文化安全关注接受照护者的体验及权力关系。公平关注需要改变哪些不平等障碍。反种族主义要求在个人互动或制度流程中出现种族主义时采取行动。

00:00:56.928 --> 00:01:12.168
The school contrasts sympathy with empathy. Sympathy expresses concern for someone; empathy tries to understand their perspective. Concern is not automatically harmful, but pity can make the person feel reduced to a problem.
学校对比sympathy与empathy。前者表达对他人的关切，后者尝试理解其视角。关切本身并非有害，但怜悯可能使人觉得自己只剩下一个问题标签。

00:01:12.168 --> 00:01:23.520
You cannot know exactly how another person feels. Say what you noticed and invite correction: You seem worried about leaving your belongings. Is that part of what is making this difficult?
你无法确切知道他人感受。可以描述观察并允许纠正：“你好像担心离开自己的物品。这是不是让你感到困难的部分原因？”

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:38.856
Compassion adds an appropriate action. With the patient’s agreement, help identify how important belongings could remain secure while assessment continues. Do not promise storage, transport or reimbursement that you cannot arrange.
Compassion把理解变为适当行动。经患者同意，可在继续评估时帮助商量如何保管重要物品。不能承诺自己无法安排的寄存、转运或赔偿。

00:01:38.856 --> 00:01:50.856
Avoid comparing the patient with your own experience or immediately correcting their emotion. The learning target is observable listening and useful support, not performing a reassuring speech.
避免拿自己的经历作比较，或立即纠正患者情绪。学习目标是可观察的倾听及实际支持，不是表演一段安慰讲话。

00:01:50.856 --> 00:02:06.432
A uniform, stretcher, police presence, pain, language difference or previous harmful health-care experience can make an ordinary question feel coercive. The patient may have less control over movement, privacy and pace.
制服、担架、警察在场、疼痛、语言差异或以往的不良医疗经历，都可能让普通问题显得带有强迫性。患者对移动、隐私及节奏的控制可能较少。

00:02:06.432 --> 00:02:21.288
Before interpreting hesitation as non-cooperation, ask what barrier, fear, symptom or prior experience could explain it. Reflection does not delay emergency care; it improves how that care is offered.
在把迟疑解释为“不配合”前，先问可能有哪些障碍、恐惧、症状或既往经历。反思不会拖延急救，而是帮助我们更好地提供照护。

00:02:21.288 --> 00:02:32.880
AVS is the school’s communication prompt: acknowledge, validate and support. Use it as a flexible sequence, not a script that every patient must accept.
AVS是学校的沟通提示：承认所表达的问题、认可感受、提供支持。应灵活运用，不是要求每位患者接受的固定台词。

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:45.288
An original response might be: You are concerned that nobody will hear your request. Being overlooked would be frustrating. I can listen to the main concern first and then explain what our assessment can offer.
原创回应可以是：“你担心自己的要求没人听见。被忽略确实会让人沮丧。我可以先听最重要的担忧，再解释我们的评估能提供什么。”

00:02:45.288 --> 00:02:58.536
Validating distress does not mean confirming a false accusation, agreeing with a delusion or accepting a threat. You can recognize fear while remaining honest about what you know and what conduct is safe.
认可痛苦，不等于确认错误指控、赞同妄想或接受威胁。可以承认恐惧，同时如实说明已知信息及安全行为边界。

00:02:58.536 --> 00:03:13.680
Check the effect. If tension rises, reduce demands, reconsider distance and seek support as indicated. Communication can improve an encounter; it never guarantees cooperation or removes a real hazard.
要观察效果。若紧张加重，应减少要求、重新考虑距离，并按需请求支持。沟通可改善互动，却不保证合作，也不会消除真实危险。

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:24.720
Equal treatment gives everyone the same step. Equitable care asks whether the same step is actually accessible and whether an avoidable barrier is creating a different outcome.
平等对待是给每个人同一步骤；公平照护则会问这一步骤是否人人都能实现，以及可避免的障碍是否造成不同结果。

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:39.600
Social determinants of health include conditions such as housing, income, education, food security, social support and access to care. They shape risk and choices, but they do not define a person or predict what they value.
健康社会决定因素包括住房、收入、教育、食物保障、社会支持及医疗可及性等条件。它们影响风险和选择，却不能定义一个人，也不能预测其价值观。

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:51.864
The school uses a five-domain organizer for social determinants. Learn those five names for this module, but do not mistake this teaching model for the only Canadian classification of health determinants.
学校使用五领域框架组织健康社会决定因素。本模块要学会这五个名称，但不能把这个教学模型当作加拿大唯一分类。

00:03:51.864 --> 00:04:08.208
Economic stability concerns resources for necessities. Health-care access and quality concern obtaining suitable services. A patient may have provincial coverage yet still face a transport, appointment, medication-cost or communication barrier.
经济稳定涉及基本生活所需资源；医疗可及性及质量涉及能否取得合适服务。患者即使有省级保障，仍可能面对交通、预约、药费或沟通障碍。

00:04:08.208 --> 00:04:24.576
Education access and quality concern learning opportunities and usable information. Do not infer intelligence or understanding from schooling: pain, unfamiliar terminology, hearing, language and stress can affect anyone’s comprehension.
教育可及性及质量涉及学习机会及可用信息。不能由学历推断智力或理解能力；疼痛、陌生术语、听力、语言及压力，都可能影响任何人的理解。

00:04:24.576 --> 00:04:42.168
Neighbourhood and built environment include housing, transport and local conditions. Social and community context include relationships, inclusion and support. These domains interact; use them to discover a barrier, not to diagnose a person’s character.
社区及建成环境包括住房、交通和当地条件；社会与社区情境包括关系、融入及支持。这些领域相互作用，应用来发现障碍，而不是诊断个人品格。

00:04:42.168 --> 00:04:53.712
Intersectionality is a way to notice how more than one social position or system can shape a person’s options at the same time. It is a question prompt, not a label to apply to someone.
交叉性是一种观察方式，用来发现多个社会位置或制度如何同时影响一个人的选择。它是提问提示，不是贴在患者身上的标签。

00:04:53.712 --> 00:05:07.176
A patient with limited mobility who lives far from services and has no phone may face a different follow-up barrier than a patient with the same diagnosis and reliable transport. Ask what is true for this person today.
行动不便、住得离服务点远且没有电话的患者，后续照护障碍可能不同于同诊断但有可靠交通的人。要询问今天这位患者的实际情况。

00:05:07.176 --> 00:05:23.088
In an original case, a patient says the clinic’s text-message instructions are unusable. Do not chart refusal or lack of motivation before finding out why. They may have a dead device, low vision, a language need or no private access.
原创案例中，患者说诊所短信说明无法使用。未查明原因前，不要记为拒绝或缺乏动力。可能是设备没电、低视力、语言需求，或没有私密使用条件。

00:05:23.088 --> 00:05:37.608
Ask one relevant question at a time: Which part prevents you using this plan? Ask permission before involving another person or viewing private messages. Do not collect unrelated financial or immigration details.
每次问一个相关问题：“这个计划的哪一部分让你无法使用？”邀请他人参与或查看私人短信前先获许可。不要收集无关财务或移民资料。

00:05:37.608 --> 00:05:51.912
Offer feasible options through approved pathways, such as a clearer explanation or a suitable communication format. A support person may help if the patient wants them involved. Do not invent a referral service or guarantee an appointment.
通过获准渠道提供可行选项，例如更清晰讲解或合适沟通格式。患者愿意时，可由支持者协助。不能虚构转介服务，也不能保证预约。

00:05:51.912 --> 00:06:04.776
Close with the actual plan and the unresolved barrier. An equitable response is not merely identifying disadvantage; it is making a useful adjustment and checking whether the patient can use it.
结束时说明实际安排及未解决障碍。公平回应不只是识别不利处境，而是作出有用调整，并确认患者能否使用。

00:06:04.776 --> 00:06:18.432
A therapeutic relationship is professional, purposeful and time-limited. Warmth supports care, but it does not remove consent, confidentiality, scope or documentation responsibilities.
治疗性关系具有专业性、目的性和时限性。温和有助照护，但不能取代同意、保密、执业范围或记录责任。

00:06:18.432 --> 00:06:31.368
Introduce your role, explain what you would like to do, ask permission, and make space for questions. If urgent care limits a choice, state the reason plainly and offer the choices that remain.
介绍自己的角色，说明拟做事项，征求许可并留出提问空间。若紧急照护限制了某项选择，要清楚说明原因，并提供仍可选择的方案。

00:06:31.368 --> 00:07:00.672
The school groups a therapeutic environment under five pillars: comfort, dignity, privacy, engagement and safety. Comfort asks what physical or sensory burden can be reduced. Dignity concerns respectful treatment and identity. Privacy concerns exposure and information. Engagement means the patient participates rather than being talked over. Safety includes the patient and crew, not merely a quiet room.
学校把治疗性环境归为五项支柱：comfort舒适、dignity尊严、privacy隐私、engagement参与、safety安全。舒适关注可减轻哪些身体或感官负担；尊严涉及尊重及身份；隐私涉及暴露及信息；参与意味着患者能够发言和决定，而非被他人抢答；安全包括患者与人员，不只是房间安静。

00:07:00.672 --> 00:07:29.784
Apply all five to the community-centre encounter. Ask whether a warmer or less noisy position would help; use the patient’s preferred name; reduce unnecessary exposure and overhearing; invite their main concern and check your explanation. Before moving, confirm safe access, observation and exits with your partner. An adjustment can support several pillars, but must not sacrifice urgent care to complete a comfort checklist.
把五项用于社区中心案例：询问较暖或较少噪声的位置是否有帮助；使用患者偏好称呼；减少不必要暴露及旁听；邀请本人说明主要担忧，并核对自己的解释。移动前与搭档确认通行、观察及出口安全。一项调整可支持多个支柱，但不能为了完成舒适清单而牺牲急救。

00:07:29.784 --> 00:08:06.576
Privacy is practical: explain the measurement and contact, ask permission, expose only the required area, and shield the patient from unnecessary observers. Ask how they wish a support person to participate rather than treating that person as the automatic decision-maker. Speak where others cannot unnecessarily overhear and protect records. A curtain protects visual privacy but does not make a conversation inaudible. Necessary communication for care should be accurate and appropriately limited, not omitted in the name of privacy.
隐私是具体做法：解释测量和接触、征求许可、只暴露需要部位，并避免不必要旁观。应询问患者希望支持者如何参与，不自动把支持者当决策者。交谈要避免他人无必要听见，记录也须保护。帘子保护视觉，却不会让谈话自动隔音。必要照护沟通应准确并适度限定，不能以隐私为由不交接。

00:08:06.576 --> 00:08:40.848
The book mentions fifteen seconds for hand gel and washing. Keep the methods separate: current CDC clinical guidance emphasizes enough alcohol hand rub to cover every surface and rubbing until dry, usually about twenty seconds. Its soap-and-water guidance allows at least fifteen seconds and also recognizes twenty-second recommendations. Do not call every fifteen-second wash wrong, or stop rubbing a still-wet product just because a timer rang. Follow the actual product and local infection-control method.
教材提到手消毒凝胶及洗手十五秒，应区分方法。现行CDC临床指导强调足量酒精手消毒液覆盖全部表面并揉至干，通常约二十秒；其肥皂流水指导接受至少十五秒，也认可二十秒建议。不能把所有十五秒洗手都说错，也不能计时一响就停止揉仍湿的产品。须按实际产品及本地感染控制方法。

00:08:40.848 --> 00:08:52.968
Do not infer language, beliefs, family roles, pain expression, eye contact or touch preferences from appearance or group membership. Ask the individual and confirm before acting.
不要根据外貌或群体身份推断语言、信仰、家庭角色、疼痛表达、眼神接触或触碰偏好。应询问本人，并在行动前确认。

00:08:52.968 --> 00:09:07.200
Use a qualified interpreter when available and appropriate. Speak to the patient, use short direct sentences, pause for interpretation, and avoid asking children to interpret sensitive or high-stakes information.
在可获得且合适时使用合格口译员。直接对患者说话，使用简短句子，给口译留出时间；敏感或高风险信息不应让儿童代译。

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:18.120
Replace jargon with a short explanation. Instead of only saying that we need a baseline, explain that you want to learn what is normal for this person so that a new change is not missed.
把术语换成简短解释。不要只说需要baseline，而应说明想知道患者平常状况，以免漏掉新变化。

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:31.776
After one important idea, ask an open question about the action: To check that I explained the next step clearly, how will you tell the receiving team what changed today? A yes to Do you understand is weaker evidence.
讲完一个重要概念后，开放式询问行动：“为了确认我解释清楚，你会怎样告诉接收团队今天发生了什么变化？”只对“听懂了吗”回答是，证据较弱。

00:09:31.776 --> 00:09:46.512
If the explanation comes back differently, take responsibility for clarifying. Rephrase, demonstrate or use appropriate interpretation; then ask again without blame. Repeating the same jargon louder is not a repair.
若复述与原意不同，应承担澄清责任。换说法、示范或使用合适口译，再不带责备地询问。把同一术语说得更大声，不算修复。

00:09:46.512 --> 00:10:00.768
Teach-back supports communication. It is not a stand-alone capacity test or a demand that an exhausted patient perform a lesson before receiving urgent care. Match the check to the person and the immediate clinical situation.
Teach-back支持沟通，不是独立的决定能力测试，也不是要求疲惫患者先完成课堂任务才能得到急救。应按个人及即时临床情况选择确认方式。

00:10:00.768 --> 00:10:31.752
The opening page also shows OARS from motivational interviewing: open questions, affirmations, reflections and summaries. Begin with an invitation rather than a presumed answer; acknowledge a genuine effort or strength, reflect the meaning tentatively, then summarize and invite correction. This is not praise for obedience or a technique for making someone choose your preference. Use focused closed questions too when an urgent fact needs a precise answer.
指定开头页还显示动机式访谈OARS：开放提问、肯定、反映及总结。应以邀请而非预设答案开始，肯定真实努力或优势，试探性地回应含义，再总结并允许纠正。这不是表扬服从，也不是让人选择你偏好方案的技巧。紧急事实需要明确答案时，也应使用重点封闭问题。

00:10:31.752 --> 00:11:03.792
Evaluate communication as a feedback loop: set a purpose, speak or listen, observe the response, check the intended meaning, and revise. If the person repeats a concern you thought was settled, ask what remains unclear rather than repeating your explanation louder. Teach-back can check whether your explanation was usable. Success means understanding and a safer, workable interaction; agreement, calmness or acceptance of transport alone does not prove it.
应以反馈循环评价沟通：确定目的、表达或倾听、观察回应、核对原意、再修正。若对方重复你以为已解决的担忧，应询问仍有什么不清楚，而不是更大声重复解释。复述确认可检查你的说明是否可用。成功指理解及更安全、可行的互动；同意、安静或接受转运本身都不证明沟通成功。

00:11:03.792 --> 00:11:20.448
Ask which language or communication method works best; do not select it from the person’s name or appearance. Use the approved professional language service and explain its role. Spoken-language interpretation and sign-language access are not the same request.
询问最适合的语言或沟通方式，不能从姓名或外貌决定。使用获准专业语言服务并解释其角色。口语口译与手语支持不是同一种请求。

00:11:20.448 --> 00:11:34.728
Speak to the patient rather than asking the interpreter to tell them everything. Use one short, complete thought, then pause. Avoid side conversations that exclude the patient or several questions bundled into one turn.
直接对患者说，而不是让口译员替自己包办讲话。每次表达一个简短完整意思，再停顿。避免把患者排除在外的旁谈，也不要一口气叠加多个问题。

00:11:34.728 --> 00:11:52.488
Ask the patient how a chosen support person should participate. Support and professional interpretation have different roles. A relative may provide history with permission, but that does not establish accurate, private interpretation of consent or sensitive concerns.
询问患者希望所选支持者怎样参与。支持与专业口译角色不同。亲属可经许可提供病史，但这不代表对同意或敏感问题的口译准确且私密。

00:11:52.488 --> 00:12:09.600
Check understanding through interpretation and document the mode used and material limits. If communication cannot be established during an urgent problem, use current emergency procedures and consultation; do not fabricate agreement or a fluent conversation.
通过口译确认理解，并记录使用方式及重要局限。若紧急问题中无法建立沟通，应使用现行急救流程及咨询；不能虚构同意或流畅对话。

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:23.256
Body position, eye contact, silence and proximity can carry different meanings for different people. A single cue does not establish hostility, consent, deception or a psychiatric condition.
身体姿势、眼神、沉默和距离，对不同的人可能有不同含义。单一线索不能证明敌意、同意、欺骗或精神疾病。

00:12:23.256 --> 00:12:36.744
Describe what you observed without judgment, then ask. A check-in protects the relationship and may reveal pain, fear, sensory overload, a need for more space or simply a personal preference.
不带评判地描述观察到的现象，然后询问。确认可以保护关系，也可能发现疼痛、恐惧、感官过载、需要更大空间，或只是个人偏好。

00:12:36.744 --> 00:12:51.096
Approach at a pace that permits the person to notice you. Introduce movement before reaching toward equipment or the patient. Visible hands and a relaxed posture can reduce uncertainty, but their meaning must still be checked.
以患者来得及注意到你的速度接近。伸手取设备或接触患者前先说明动作。双手可见、姿势放松可减少不确定性，但仍应确认其实际感受。

00:12:51.096 --> 00:13:06.312
If safe, avoid towering over a seated person. Use a non-confrontational angle and appropriate distance while keeping a clear exit. Do not crouch into an unsafe position, block the patient’s route or let a crowd surround them.
安全时避免居高临下地站在坐着的人面前。采用不具对抗性的角度及适当距离，并保留清晰退出路线。不能蹲到不安全位置、堵住患者通道，或让人群包围患者。

00:13:06.312 --> 00:13:22.176
Reduce noise, unnecessary personnel and exposure where feasible. Ask before changing lighting or moving a support person. A quiet room is helpful only if access, observation and clinical care remain safe.
可行时减少噪声、无关人员及身体暴露。改变灯光或让支持者离开前应询问。安静空间只有在通行、观察及照护仍安全时才有帮助。

00:13:22.176 --> 00:13:37.200
Silence, eye contact and personal space do not have one universal meaning. Ask whether your position works for this person and adapt to hearing, vision, mobility and expressed preferences rather than demanding a performance of respect.
沉默、眼神及个人距离没有唯一通用含义。询问自己的位置是否合适，并按听力、视力、行动及明确偏好调整，而不是要求患者以某种表现证明尊重。

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:49.728
Trauma-informed practice recognizes that distress may be linked to previous or current harm. It does not require the patient to tell a trauma story, and it does not diagnose trauma from behavior.
创伤知情实践承认痛苦可能与过去或当前伤害有关，但不要求患者讲述创伤经历，也不根据行为诊断创伤。

00:13:49.728 --> 00:14:01.128
Predictability can help: announce movement before touching, explain the monitor, offer a less exposed position, and let the person choose which safe arm is examined first.
可预测性有帮助：触碰前先告知动作，说明监护仪用途，提供更有隐私的姿势，并让患者选择先检查哪一只安全的手臂。

00:14:01.128 --> 00:14:14.616
A raised voice or fearful expression does not by itself establish violence. Describe behaviour and context rather than labeling the person aggressive because of a cultural difference, frustration or a refusal.
声音提高或面露恐惧，本身不证明暴力。应描述行为及情境，不能因为文化差异、沮丧或拒绝，就把患者标成有攻击性。

00:14:14.616 --> 00:14:31.320
Specific threatening actions, a weapon or rapidly worsening behaviour can change scene safety. Maintain a route away, coordinate with your partner and request the appropriate resources. A compassionate approach does not require staying in an uncontrolled threat.
具体威胁动作、武器或行为迅速恶化，都可改变现场安全。应保持撤离路线、与搭档协调并请求适当资源。关怀不要求留在未控制的威胁中。

00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:46.824
BCEHS G01 also directs attention to medical contributors such as hypoxia, hypoglycemia, head injury, drug effects or infection. Do not let a psychiatric label or a conflict distract from assessment of a new clinical change.
BCEHS G01也要求关注医学因素，如缺氧、低血糖、头伤、药物作用或感染。不能因精神科标签或冲突，而忽略新发临床变化的评估。

00:14:46.824 --> 00:15:02.664
Continue safe communication while assessment and support are arranged. This lesson does not grant detention, restraint or medication authority. Those decisions need the current legal and service pathway, not a communication mnemonic.
安排评估与支持时继续安全沟通。本课不赋予拘留、约束或用药权限；这些决定必须依现行法律及机构流程，不能靠沟通口诀。

00:15:02.664 --> 00:15:18.816
At a fictional community-centre entrance, several people answer over a patient who asks everyone to back away. If safe, stop advancing, create space and arrange one clinician to speak. Do not begin by demanding that the patient calm down.
在虚构社区中心入口，多人抢着替患者回答，患者要求大家退后。安全时应停止接近、留出空间，并安排一名人员讲话。不要一开始就命令患者冷静。

00:15:18.816 --> 00:15:31.080
Try: I will stay here while you tell me the main concern. What would you like us to hear first? Then pause long enough for an answer. Acknowledge the concern before moving to the next assessment question.
可以说：“你讲最重要的担忧时，我先留在这里。你最想让我们先听到什么？”随后留出回答时间。先承认该担忧，再进入下一个评估问题。

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:45.216
Offer a genuine small choice: We can explain the check here, or in that quieter area if it is safe to move. Do not offer a choice that has already been decided, and do not bargain away necessary safety controls.
提供真实小选择：“我们可以在这里解释检查；如果移动安全，也可以去较安静处。”不能提供早已决定好的假选择，也不能拿必要安全控制作交换。

00:15:45.216 --> 00:16:01.248
If the person says no, clarify what was declined and reassess the situation. If distress or danger rises, change the plan and obtain support. A failed first phrase is information, not a reason to become punitive.
患者说不时，应确认拒绝的是哪部分，再复评。若痛苦或危险加重，应调整计划并取得支持。第一句话无效是信息，不是转为惩罚性态度的理由。

00:16:01.248 --> 00:16:14.928
If a patient reports discriminatory treatment, do not debate whether the experience “counts.” Listen, acknowledge the concern, clarify what the person needs now and take a practical step within your role.
患者报告遭遇歧视时，不要争辩这段经历“算不算”。先倾听、承认其担忧，确认当下需要，并在职责范围内采取实际行动。

00:16:14.928 --> 00:16:29.760
If a colleague’s conduct creates immediate risk, prioritize patient safety, speak up through the appropriate chain and document objective events under service policy. Do not promise confidentiality or a particular investigation result.
若同事行为造成即时风险，应优先保障患者安全，按适当渠道提出，并依服务政策客观记录事件。不要保证绝对保密或承诺调查结果。

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:46.032
The school and FNHA frame Indigenous cultural safety in the context of colonial harms, racism and unequal power in care. This context helps explain why a service must earn trust rather than expect automatic trust in a uniform.
学校及FNHA把原住民文化安全置于殖民伤害、种族主义及照护权力不平等背景中。这个背景说明机构为何应争取信任，而不是期待制服自动带来信任。

00:16:46.032 --> 00:17:00.768
Do not assume that every Indigenous patient has the same history, beliefs, family structure or preferred support. First Nations, Inuit and Metis identities are distinct, and individual preferences still need to be asked.
不能假定每位原住民患者有相同历史、信仰、家庭结构或支持偏好。First Nations、Inuit及Metis身份各有区别，仍须询问个人偏好。

00:17:00.768 --> 00:17:14.784
Ask whether there is someone or something important to include in the present care, without requiring a trauma narrative or proof of identity. Explore feasible patient-chosen support and explain clinical limits transparently.
可以询问当前照护是否应纳入某位重要支持者或重要需求，但不能要求讲创伤故事或证明身份。应探讨患者选择的可行支持，并透明说明临床限制。

00:17:14.784 --> 00:17:31.368
If a discriminatory assumption is diverting attention from symptoms, redirect toward the patient’s actual findings and needs. Support the affected person and use the appropriate accountability route. Good intentions do not certify that the interaction felt safe.
若歧视性假设让注意力偏离症状，应转回患者实际发现及需求。支持受影响者，并使用适当问责渠道。良好本意不能证明互动令人感到安全。

00:17:31.368 --> 00:18:02.352
School 1B names residential schools, the Sixties Scoop, Indian hospitals and the In Plain Sight review. Residential schools separated children from family and suppressed culture. The Sixties Scoop involved removal of Indigenous children into non-Indigenous care. Indian hospitals were part of segregated health care. In Plain Sight examines Indigenous-specific racism in British Columbia health care. These are distinct subjects, not interchangeable names for one event.
学校1B点名寄宿学校、Sixties Scoop、Indian hospitals及In Plain Sight审查。寄宿学校使儿童与家庭分离并压制文化；Sixties Scoop涉及把原住民儿童带离并安置到非原住民照护中；Indian hospitals属于隔离医疗体系的一部分；In Plain Sight审视BC医疗中的原住民特定种族主义。这些是不同主题，不能当作同一事件的不同名称。

00:18:02.352 --> 00:18:32.064
Use that context to examine the power and assumptions in your own encounter. It does not prove that this patient experienced a particular event or explains their symptoms. In the existing guarded-patient case, ask what would help now, preserve the medical assessment and offer patient-chosen support when feasible. Challenge a discriminatory shortcut with actual findings, and use the appropriate accountability route. Do not require the patient to disclose trauma or teach you their history.
应以这个背景检查当前互动中的权力及自身假设；它不证明眼前患者经历过某事件，也不能解释其症状。在现有戒备患者案例中，询问现在什么有帮助，保留医学评估，并在可行时提供患者选择的支持。用真实发现纠正歧视性捷径，并使用适当问责渠道。不能要求患者披露创伤或负责教授自己的历史。

00:18:32.064 --> 00:18:45.144
If you mispronounce a name, expose someone without warning or dismiss a concern, a brief repair can reduce additional harm. Avoid centering your intent or asking the patient to reassure you.
若叫错姓名、未经提醒暴露患者或轻视其担忧，简短修复能减少进一步伤害。不要把重点放在自己的本意，也不要要求患者安慰你。

00:18:45.144 --> 00:18:57.456
Accountability includes follow-through. If the person requests a different clinician, interpreter, support person or complaint route, explore what is feasible and explain any limit honestly.
承担责任还包括后续行动。若患者要求换一位医护、使用口译员、增加支持者或了解投诉渠道，应探讨可行性并诚实说明限制。

00:18:57.456 --> 00:19:12.888
The school uses PACE for speaking up with a colleague: probe, alert, challenge and emergency. It gives increasing clarity when a softer message is not heard; it does not require you to wait through four stages during imminent harm.
学校用PACE提示向同事提出问题：探询、提醒、明确挑战及紧急行动。当较柔和信息未被听见时，表达逐步明确；迫在眉睫的伤害不要求先走完四级。

00:19:12.888 --> 00:19:25.944
An original probe is: Would one speaker and more space help this interview? An alert adds the effect: Our repeated interruptions are increasing distress and preventing us hearing the symptoms.
原创探询可以是：“改成一人讲话并多留空间，会不会更有利于访谈？”提醒则加上影响：“我们反复打断正在加重痛苦，也妨碍听取症状。”

00:19:25.944 --> 00:19:41.136
A challenge is direct: Stop using that label; describe the finding we actually assessed. If immediate harm is developing, use the safe intervention, supervisor or emergency support pathway appropriate to your role and the scene.
明确挑战是：“停止使用那个标签，描述我们真正检查到的发现。”若即时伤害正在形成，应按角色及现场情况，使用安全干预、主管或紧急支持路径。

00:19:41.136 --> 00:19:55.296
Speaking up is not permission to physically confront a colleague or abandon another patient. Preserve care, communicate the changed assignment and document relevant facts through the correct process after the immediate problem is controlled.
提出问题不等于获准与同事发生肢体冲突或抛下另一患者。应维持照护、沟通任务变更，并在即时问题受控后按流程记录相关事实。

00:19:55.296 --> 00:20:08.544
A patient with new confusion after a fall says, “No one touches me.” A family member asks you to force an examination. The patient is alert but guarded; no immediate airway threat is visible.
一名跌倒后新发意识混乱的患者说“谁也别碰我”。家属要求你强行检查。患者清醒但戒备，暂未见即时气道威胁。

00:20:08.544 --> 00:20:25.200
Do not infer incapacity from the refusal or appearance. Explain the concern, ask permission to talk, offer privacy and choices, use the communication support the patient prefers, and assess whether an emergency response or consultation is required.
不能因为拒绝或外表就推断缺乏决定能力。说明担忧、征求交谈许可、提供隐私和选择、采用患者偏好的沟通支持，并判断是否需要紧急处置或咨询。

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:38.136
A useful reflection names a behavior, its impact and the next change. “I was culturally sensitive” is not observable; “I asked how the patient wanted the family involved” can be observed and improved.
有效反思要写明行为、影响及下一步改变。“我有文化敏感性”无法观察；“我询问患者希望家属如何参与”则可观察并改进。

00:20:38.136 --> 00:20:49.272
These prompts prepare for class discussion, not a self-certification. Practice with an instructor and request feedback from the person receiving care whenever it is appropriate and safe.
这些提示用于课堂讨论，不构成自我认证。应在教师指导下练习，并在适当且安全时向接受照护者征求反馈。

00:20:49.272 --> 00:21:03.144
Anchoring means an early explanation holds too strongly. If a dispatch label says intoxication, a new focal weakness must still change your assessment. The initial label is not the patient’s diagnosis.
锚定偏差是过度抓住早期解释。即使派遣标签是醉酒，新发局灶无力仍必须改变评估。初始标签不是患者诊断。

00:21:03.144 --> 00:21:16.920
Confirmation bias means favouring information that supports what you already think. Ask what finding would make the explanation wrong, then look for it through the appropriate assessment rather than collecting only agreeing details.
确认偏差是偏爱支持既有想法的信息。应问什么发现会推翻该解释，再通过适当评估寻找，而不是只收集相符细节。

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:31.992
Attribution bias can turn a missed appointment into a judgment about character. Ask about the actual access problem. A transport barrier and a lack of concern are different explanations; neither should be invented without evidence.
归因偏差可能把错过预约变成人品判断。应询问实际就医障碍。交通问题与不关心自身健康是不同解释，两者都不能无证据编造。

00:21:31.992 --> 00:21:46.800
For class rehearsal, an observer should hear the question, see the adjustment and identify the reassessment. Reflection is useful when it changes the next behaviour; merely saying I have no bias does not demonstrate a skill.
课堂演练中，观察者应能听到问题、看到调整，并指出复评。反思只有改变下一行为才有用；只说“我没有偏见”不能证明技能。
